id: core/relationship
title: "First-class Relationship"
kind: ontology-contract
record_shape: header
status: draft
version: 0.1.0
updated: 2026-09-30
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex, reconciling the relationship-core proposal on behalf of the maintainer"

purpose: >
  Define the generic Relationship record that lets YAWN preserve a situated,
  revisable relation without confusing it with a URL, a structural Yawn edge,
  a coupling mechanism, a permission, or a participant roster.

definition:
  relationship: >
    A stable, revisable instance of situated relation among one or more
    addressable referents. It carries the context needed to inspect how the
    relation is understood and changes over time: participation, stakes,
    coupling, boundaries, policy references, attributed claims, events, and
    open questions.
  identity_rule: >
    A Relationship has an identity independent of any displayed route, View,
    embedding, or Yawn that may steward it. Multiple directional Views may
    enter the same Relationship.
  record_rule: >
    A relationship record is an inspectable projection of the relation, not a
    complete account of the people, institutions, traditions, or reality it
    references.

facets:
  referent: "A person, agent, group, institution, concept, tradition, source corpus, artifact, or other addressable thing."
  participation: "A referent's time- and episode-specific involvement, role, standpoint, and presence in this Relationship."
  coupling: "A channel or mechanism through which information or effects can flow."
  boundary: "What is protected, admitted, excluded, or allowed to cross."
  policy_or_contract: "Explicit permissions, prohibitions, duties, commitments, conditions, and decision rights that govern possible action."
  arena: "A current situational field in which part of the Relationship is active."
  yawn: "A durable orientation contract that may steward this Relationship when continuity, inquiry, proof, or maintenance warrants it."
  structural_relation: "A typed Yawn-to-Yawn graph edge used by the holarchy; it is not this generic Relationship."

must_remain_distinct:
  - "relationship is not coupling: an effect may be technically possible and still prohibited."
  - "relationship is not policy or authority: a policy governs an action within a relation; it does not exhaust the relation."
  - "relationship is not participation: a historical author, source, or modeled voice is not thereby a present participant."
  - "relationship is not a Yawn: a relation earns a Yawn only when it needs independent continuity, inquiry, proof, or stewardship."
  - "relationship is not a structural Relation: agency-holarchy Relation remains a Yawn-to-Yawn lateral edge."
  - "relationship is not a slash: the slash opens or traverses a Relation Address View."

views:
  stable_subject: relationship
  selectable_apertures:
    - purpose
    - model
    - perspectives
    - sources
    - boundaries
    - history
    - frontier
  independent_coordinates:
    - resolution
    - effective_time
    - scope
    - standpoint
  rule: >
    Changing an aperture, resolution, time, scope, or standpoint changes the
    permitted View, never the canonical Relationship identity or authority.

inference_envelope:
  rule: >
    An inference need not reproduce the same interpretation forever, but its
    envelope MUST preserve the source version, generator, recorded time,
    model or policy version when available, epistemic status, confidence,
    active Relationship and standpoint, supersession state, and disclosure
    boundary.
  replay: "Historical replay uses persisted records and events; it does not silently regenerate a past interpretation."
  schema: schemas/inference-envelope.v0.1.schema.json

relationship_yawn_rule: >
  A Relationship may be promoted to or stewarded by a Yawn only through an
  explicit proposal and applicable authority. The reason must name an
  independently meaningful purpose, scope, authority or privacy boundary,
  proof obligation, maintenance loop, or recurring inquiry.

boundaries:
  - "A relationship record does not establish agreement, consent, truth, identity, or authority by itself."
  - "A relationship record does not infer a participant's private state or belief without attributable source and permission."
  - "A relationship record does not turn a historical speaker, quoted author, or modeled perspective into a present participant."
  - "Embedding proximity, path nesting, or topical similarity do not create containment, identity, consent, or authorization."

links:
  - schemas/relationship.v0.1.schema.json
  - schemas/participation.v0.1.schema.json
  - schemas/relation-address.v0.1.schema.json
  - schemas/inference-envelope.v0.1.schema.json
  - core/relation-address.yawn
  - core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
  - core/holarchy.yawn
  - spec/ontology.md

proof:
  covers: [definition, facets, must_remain_distinct, views, inference_envelope, relationship_yawn_rule, boundaries]
  tests:
    - tests/relationship-core-v0.1.test.mjs
  fixtures:
    - fixtures/relationship-core.v0.1.json
  status: proposed-until-maintainer-review
